{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Purpose\nDurable register of parentless open bugs whose rebar-debug investigation reaches the not-a-bug or design-choice escalation bar. Keep unresolved decisions here so the operator can resolve them together without losing root-cause context. Each bug retains its detailed evidence and RCA on its own ticket.\n\n## Pending decisions\n- `afflicted-hexed-arthropods` — choose code-review invocation/enforcement semantics. Recommended compatible contract: explicit CLI/library/MCP `review-code` always runs by sending `enabled=True`; retain `verify.enable_code_review` only as the default for direct/internal verdict production; keep the Gerrit adapter explicit override because deployed receiver activation is already its enforcement control. Alternative: introduce a true `enforce_code_review` key, wire Gerrit voting to it, and coordinate repository plus deployed receiver configuration atomically so the currently-live LLM-Review gate is not silently disabled.\n- `peach-chemic-hairstreak` — choose the repository Bedrock default and provenance scope. Recommended: pin `us-east-1`, matching the measured provider overlay, CI defaults, service runbook, and compose defaults, and add truthful source metadata so provider provenance reports `repo-config`; keep `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION` higher precedence. Alternatives: pin `us-west-2` based on the local `frontier-bedrock` profile, or leave the repo unpinned and treat fresh-shell setup as an operator profile/env responsibility.\n\n## Resolved during sweep\n- `dragonish-sylphic-sheep` — preserve Chat Completions with `openai-chat:`; future Responses migration tracked by `upbeat-illadvised-springtail`.\n- `novel-unwasteful-stonefly` — user authorized broad typed validation, including enum and non-enum coercion, for this bug.\n- `stumpy-cinnabar-basenji` — spawn by default, optional caller-supplied context, importable/pickleable callable contract, fail-open serialization boundaries, and no cloudpickle/loky absent a concrete caller.\n- `paper-spiritous-halicore` — dense successful criterion banking satisfies the product contract; incremental-gap timing is an oracle-policy preference. Closed as `not_a_bug` after operator acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every unresolved not-a-bug or design-choice escalation from the sweep is listed with the exact decision required.\n- [ ] Each listed bug is linked with `relates_to` and holds its evidence on the source ticket.\n- [ ] Operator decisions move entries from Pending to Resolved with the chosen contract recorded."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787027338858541001,"uuid":"936816af-eb39-4917-9d9b-76277bedf6a7"}